   ]
  },
  "bio": [
   {
    "text": "Starving and crazed, Mavren Fein stumbled up to Fort Adanto proclaiming his faith in Saint Elenda, and Mardia had him let in.",
    "cites": [
     "race-part-1-2017-10-11-e0",
     "race-part-1-2017-10-11-e2"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/race-part-1-2017-10-11#:~:text=I%20have%20conquered%20the,itself%2C%20praise%20Saint%20Elenda%21",
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/race-part-1-2017-10-11#:~:text=Hierophant%20Mavren%20Fein%3F"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "He broke through his cell wall and fed on Manuel, ending his Blood Fast, then revealed his crew was dead and that he would continue the mission.",
    "cites": [
     "race-part-1-2017-10-11-e7",
     "race-part-1-2017-10-11-e8"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/race-part-1-2017-10-11#:~:text=A%20breath%20later%2C%20his,blood%20filled%20the%20air.",
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/race-part-1-2017-10-11#:~:text=But%20I%20intend%20to,mission%20all%20the%20same."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "At Orazca, he and Vona tackled and wounded Kumena.",
    "cites": [
     "flood-2018-01-10-e9"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/flood-2018-01-10#:~:text=The%20vampires%20scratched%20and,line%20into%20Kumena%27s%20side."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "He later sliced Vona's cheek for insulting Elenda.",
    "cites": [
     "who-tells-stories-2018-02-07-e12"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/who-tells-stories-2018-02-07#:~:text=Do%20not%20speak%20ill%20of%20a%20living%20saint%21"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "In an alternate ending, he begged Elenda's forgiveness and followed her.",
    "cites": [
     "rivals-ixalan-magic-story-alternate-endings-2018-02-21-r2"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/rivals-ixalan-magic-story-alternate-endings-2018-02-21#:~:text=Saint%20Elenda%20turned%20and,and%20Mavren%20Fein%20followed."
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "As leader of the Legion's auxiliaries, released to fight, he demanded freedom as a reward from Huatli, who said they had made no bargain.",
    "cites": [
     "three-hundred-steps-under-the-sun-r2",
     "three-hundred-steps-under-the-sun-e11"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/three-hundred-steps-under-the-sun#:~:text=the%20thin%2C%20patrician%20leader%20of%20the%20auxiliaries",
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/three-hundred-steps-under-the-sun#:~:text=We%20never%20made%20a%20bargain%2C"
    ]
   },
   {
    "text": "He helped hold the temple gate and carried the wounded Inti from the line.",
    "cites": [
     "three-hundred-steps-under-the-sun-e16",
     "three-hundred-steps-under-the-sun-e23"
    ],
    "links": [
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/three-hundred-steps-under-the-sun#:~:text=We%27ll%20hold%20the%20gate%2C",
     "https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/three-hundred-steps-under-the-sun#:~:text=A%20blood%2Dslick%20and%20oil%2Dstained,wounded%20Inti%20with%20him."
    ]
   }
  ],
  "status": {
   "text": "As of the latest story, Mavren Fein is alive and fighting alongside Huatli's company at the Winged Temple.",
   "cites": [
    "three-hundred-steps-under-the-sun-e23"
   ],
